From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:44:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Input: apple_z2: Add iPad 5 (J71t) touchscreen support
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The iPad 5 touchscreen controller (iOS AppleMultitouchN1SPI, personality
C1F15,1) runs the iPad 6's generation-1 runtime protocol: EB frames with
the alternating 1/2 sequence tag and a byte-sum checksum, a data phase
with byte 2 set to 1 and a length + 5 transfer, E3 report information
and a framed second phase for long report reads. Add it as a variant of
the J71b paths, with only what differs:

- Boot: no boot interrupt. After power-up the N1 HBPP bootloader is
  found by its NOP probe (1a a1, 18 e1 x7) and its version register
  (0x10008ffc). The firmware file supplies the unit's calibration, sent
  in packets of at most 0x3f0 bytes to 0x10009000, and the firmware
  packet; both are checked through ATN_ACK (0x4bc1), with five
  attempts. Then the N1 register calibration (fll-mval, clk32 enable
  and the N1 defaults, const-cal 2 on controller 0x434d11a0), the
  calibration request 1f 01, and the execute command (0x10003400).
- Power: the analog supply is a PMIC switch, the display sync a pin
  that moves between peripheral route 2 and the GPIO function, and
  iOS sends REQ_WAKEUP (19 c1) and the NOP probe before releasing
  reset.
- Discovery: E2 twice (not E2 then E1), the family (0xd1), sensor
  (0xd3), region (0xd0, 0xa1) and surface (0xd9) reports. Each read
  waits 2 ms first and is retried up to five times while the reply is
  corrupt; wakes within 100 ms are suppressed. The short (E6) second
  phase repeats E6, the long (E7) one keeps the first phase's checksum
  instead of recomputing it with byte 2 set.
- Runtime: the length reply is checked as a whole (E-class, checksum
  at 14); the data phase carries its checksum in the last two bytes
  rather than at 14; the data header's tag is not checked (iOS does
  not), but its length must fill the transfer.
- Reports: classic contact reports 0x43..0x45 without the HID envelope,
  with the contact offset and stride from their header. Raw Y grows
  upwards; boards set touchscreen-inverted-y.
- Timing: 10 us chip-select setup and hold, no inactive time, 25 us
  between the phases of a control command; the S8000 SPI already runs
  without an inter-word delay, as iOS' configureSPI() asks.

The interrupt switches to level-low after boot, as on J71b.

The firmware file is the model's z2fw: a configuration record, a
calibration record for multi-touch-calibration at 0x10009000 (up to
0x400 bytes) and the mtprops firmware packet, without the init and
wait-interrupt records. The bootloader copies the unit's calibration
from the ADT into apple,z2-cal-blob, as on J71b.

Signed-off-by: Berkay Kösebay <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
[Orchard: from brkosebay/linux e623b3c6, 39c86d64, b0270d0b, 8ba40b6e
 (J71t ledger 8.1, 8.2, 8.3); his separate apple_n1 driver becomes a
 J71T variant of apple_z2 that shares the J71b generation-1 runtime,
 with his protocol and timing facts as match data and small branches.
 Calibration comes from apple,z2-cal-blob and the firmware from the
 Orchard recipe instead of private files (8.4). Not carried: the stage
 and trace parameters, error dumps, the recovery worker and the
 retained-power suspend (8.11); the device is powered off over suspend
 like the other Z2 variants. Pressure is not reported.]
